## Tool batching

- Batch independent lookups into one turn instead of issuing them
  one per turn: calls issued together in the same message run
  concurrently. This matters most when a call has real latency
  (e.g. network or process round trips) — batching several such
  calls in one turn saves real seconds, not just milliseconds.
- Never batch a call whose arguments depend on a previous call's
  result in the same turn — only issue truly independent calls
  together; batching a dependent call before its input exists will
  just fail or use stale data.
